# ash command, tool, and plugin denylist
#
# This file allows you to explicitly block specific Unix commands, managed tools,
# and native plugins from being executed by ash (via run_unix_command and
# run_unix_pipeline), even if they appear in .ash_allow or are discovered in
# ~/.ash/tools/ or ~/.ash/plugins/.
#
# Format rules:
# - One command per line (preferred), or comma-separated on one line.
# - Lines starting with # are comments and are ignored.
# - Use bare executable or tool names only (no paths, no arguments).
# - Empty lines are ignored.
#
# Precedence and Safety model:
# - Denials take absolute precedence over allowlist rules: if a command is in
#   both .ash_allow and .ash_deny, it is DENIED.
# - The ASH_DENY environment variable (comma-separated) can also be used to
#   specify denied commands.
# - When you modify this file, ash install and update tools will not overwrite
#   or reset your custom denylist rules.
#
# Examples:
# To block macOS text-to-speech:
#   say
# To block a specific plugin:
#   calculator
# To block network diagnostics:
#   ping6
#   traceroute6
#
# List commands, tools, or plugins to deny below:
